  "gloss": {
    "en": "Optionally (Śākalya), a padānta aK vowel before following ṛ remains in its natural form, and the aK is (if needed) shortened (hrasva).",
    "sa": "In saṃhitā at a pada boundary, if the left ends in aK (a/ā/i/ī/u/ū/ṛ/ṝ/ḷ/ḹ) and the right begins with ṛ (ऋ/ॠ), Śākalya allows prakṛtibhāva (no vowel sandhi) and sets the left aK to hrasva; alternative derivation applies the normal vowel-sandhi rule (notably 6.1.87 for a/ā + ṛ → ar)."
  },
